course: dictionary
lesson: 8823
title: A shepherdess in a song
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shepherdess is a woman or girl who looks after sheep. She keeps the flock safe, finds grass for them and brings them home. «It's raining, shepherdess, bring in your white sheep.» The rain and the words bring in your sheep tell you her job is outdoors, with the sheep.
explain: This line is from a song from 1780, «Il pleut, il pleut, bergère». Bergère is the French word for shepherdess, so the English line uses the same idea. Old stories, nursery rhymes and paintings often show shepherdesses in the fields, like Little Bo-Peep, who lost her sheep.
explain: Today the word shepherd is often used for both men and women, so a woman can be called a shepherd too. Shepherdess is the word to use when you want to say clearly that she is a woman or girl.
fact: A shepherdess is a woman or girl who looks after sheep.
fact: «Shepherdess» can also mean a pretty figure of a shepherdess in old paintings, poems and china ornaments.
fact: «A china shepherdess» is a small ornament of a shepherdess, made of china.
fact: In the Bible, Rachel looked after her father's sheep.
fact: Today, «shepherd» is often used for both men and women.
exercise: In «It's raining, shepherdess, bring in your white sheep», what job does the shepherdess do? | Bakes cakes for the village | *Looks after sheep | Sails boats
exercise: What is a shepherdess? | A sheep with a bell | A type of cloud | A queen who lives in a castle | *A woman or girl who looks after sheep
exercise: Which word would you use for a girl who is looking after the sheep in a field? | castle | *shepherdess | river | fox
test: In old paintings and china ornaments, a shepherdess is often shown as what? | *A pretty figure | A busy shop worker | A soldier with a sword | A ship's captain
test: Today, the word «shepherd» is often used for whom? | Only girls | *Both men and women | Only sheep
exam: Which of these is a shepherdess from a story or rhyme? | *Little Bo-Peep | Snow White | Goldilocks | Cinderella
